      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The La Mesa History Center, located in the historic McKinney House Museum on University Avenue, preserves the city’s early heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityoflamesa.gov/765/Historic-Landmarks",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "La Mesa boasts several designated historic landmarks, such as the Bengston House and the Frederick and Marta Binney Ranch House.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityoflamesa.gov/765/Historic-Landmarks",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town of Harper, later Costa Mesa, grew around a siding of the Santa Ana and Newport Railway in the early 1900s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
